abstract: >-
  State-level panels of malaria and dengue counts in 34 Indian units (malaria 2002–2025,
  dengue 2007–2025), compiled from official programme documents, with ENSO indices,
  IMD-based climate exposures, population denominators, the Python pipeline that builds
  them and the R analysis (negative binomial mixed models, cross-validation, mediation
  and conditional 2026–27 scenarios) of the associated paper. Version 1.1.0 adds the
  peer-review analyses (shared temporal dependence, spatial structure, trend and
  testing-effort specifications, climate nonlinearity, pre-season validation).
